> The compiler is set to -O3
>
> Not using any matrix algebra beyond the example I posted previously.  Do you think that could be killing my performance?  If so, how would you suggest I change things?

Not sure I understand ... If your model with 200 covariates has something like

   for(i in 1:N){
        mu[i] <- 1

        + b_var_1 * var_1[i]
        + b_var_2 * var_2[i]
        + b_var_3 * var_3[i]
        ...
        + b_var_200 * var_200[i];
    }
    y ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);

then yes, that could kill the performance. The reason is that it has to do roughly 200 * N auto-diffs per evaluation of the log-posterior. Markus optimized the differentiation of the X * beta construction, so it is much better if you can write the model with as much matrix algebra as possible.

Ben

