Dear all,

Can Stan can be used to fit a clustering model with the number of clusters K to be determined? I was expecting to see a way of doing it in Stan, but as the manual says, discrete parameters are "not directly supported by Stan", and I'm not sure if this is a showstopper or not (since K is discrete, as are the cluster labels). I sketched a Stan program with a line like:

  parameters {
    ...
    int<lower=1,upper=N> clusteralloc[N]
    ...
  }

but it seems that's not going to compile since parameters must be real-valued. So I'd be grateful for any tips about how to create a Stan program that can address this kind of problem.

I imagine that one way is to relax the problem so every datum is a member of every class, having a mixture of weights, but with a sparse prior on the weights so they tend to [0,0,0,1,0,0].

I found a message from Bob implying Stan's design isn't suited for discrete parameters <https://groups.google.com/d/msg/stan-users/vVPW6Rub_3Q/fd_tHXpiAwwJ>, so maybe I should be looking elsewhere. But any tips gratefully received.

Best
Dan

