I know what you're saying but in practice it doesn't seem like such a big deal.  I'll start with 4 chains of 10 iterations to make sure the program runs ok, then go to 100.  If 100 is lightning-fast, I'll go to 1000, etc.  If it's not quite at convergence and it's no longer running in less than a couple seconds, I'll switch to doubling:  2000, 4000, etc.  Somehow that works ok.  Especially since there's no need to recompile the model each time.
Andrew

