On the point of vectorising the binomial function:

   for (n in 1:N) {
     p[n] <- (gamma + (1 - gamma) * inv_logit( f_x[n] ));
   }
   y ~ binomial(n_trials, p);

I've never been able to get this to work: stan always returns an "unknown distribution" error. I believe it's because the binomial function wants values y and n_trials to be integers, not arrays of integers (which is why it works in the loop). Perhaps the function you're using the development version hasn't been pushed to the public yet?

