gdb says the error is from diag_post_multiply(), where it looks like we have a bug that is now fixed by e68441f1fa292e4ee92a0881f8f08845d688ba45

Although, then you have indexing issues with z1

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp/SU/tds$ ./ordMultiProt_E_chol --data=datstan_mp.Rdump

Exception: INDEX OPERATOR [] OUT OF BOUNDS; index=3; lower bound=1; upper bound=2; index position=1; z1

Diagnostic information:
Dynamic exception type: std::out_of_range
std::exception::what: INDEX OPERATOR [] OUT OF BOUNDS; index=3; lower bound=1; upper bound=2; index position=1; z1

goodrich@CYBERPOWERPC:/tmp/SU/tds$ grep -n z1 ordMultiProt_E_chol.stan
73:     matrix[D1,ncut1] z1[beta];
96:     real subdiagonals_z1[ncov_D1];
103:    vector<lower=0>[D1] diagonals_z1;
142:    matrix[D1,D1] L_z1;
216:                    L_z1[j,j] <- 1;
218:                            L_z1[i,j] <- subdiagonals_z1[count];
222:                            L_z1[i,j] <- 0.0;
226:    L_z1    <- diag_post_multiply(L_z1,diagonals_z1);
269:    Zeta1           <- Zeta1_norm * transpose(L_z1);
284:      /* generate simplex, gamma1[d,1:(ncut1-1)] from standard normals, z1[d,1:(ncut2-1),1:beta] */
285:      for( c in 1:ncut1 ) gamma1_u[d,c] <- dot_self(z1[d,c]); /* each z1[d,c] is of length beta */
362:    subdiagonals_z1 ~ normal(0.0, 1.0);
370:    diagonals_z1    ~ cauchy(0,5);
384:    for( d in 1:D1) for( c in 1:ncut1 ) z1[d,c]     ~ normal(0,1);

Ben

P.S. We need a chose(N,K) function to avoid making the user utilize integer division.

