>
>         P.S. We need a chose(N,K) function to avoid making the user utilize integer division.
>
>
>     binomial_coefficient_log() will compute the choose function. See page 143 of the manual (v1.1.0).
>
>
> But the output is a double. Thus, exp(binomial_coefficient_log(K,2)) is right (albeit verbose), but the parser considers
> it illegal for the index when declaring the size of a matrix.
